of the vegan cheese melted on top. :)\n\nWe got the portobello tamale which we both liked. We loved the corn and kale that the tamale had in it along with the salsa that was on top.  \n\nWe loved the salsa so much so we asked for an extra salsa on the side, that we added on top of everything!\n\nWe also got the taco cuete, which we both weren't that big of a fan of because we didn't like the sauce on it. \n\nOverall I will go back to this place again to try something new like the burrito or the ceviche! The people who worked there were friendly and very helpful in helping us pick out what to get. \n\nEven if you aren't vegan you will like this place because it's full of flavor and spice! Check it out if your looking for a healthy plant based mexican meal."}],"state":"CA"}", "original_answer": "Based on the provided structured data, Taco Tuyo is a local business in Santa Barbara, California that offers a variety of vegan and non-vegan Mexican dishes through its food truck and online delivery services. The business has received mixed reviews from customers, with some praising its unique and flavorful dishes, while others have criticized the service and food quality.

